<header class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">SPARQL workbench · local build</p>
  <h1>One query. CPU and GPU together.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Load RDF, edit a query and inspect the joins that actually ran. The same query API chooses eligible GPU joins and completes the remaining work on the CPU.</p>
  <div class="hero-tags"><span>RDF stays in the engine</span><span>Checked GPU readbacks</span><span>No npm release required</span></div>
</header>

<section class="panel runtime-panel" id="runtime" aria-labelledby="runtime-title">
  <div class="panel-title"><h2 id="runtime-title">1. Local runtime</h2><span id="webgpu-status" class="badge">Checking WebGPU exposure…</span></div>
  <p>The default module is this site's copy of the repository. Its matching Wasm build must include the mixed query operations. No CDN package is loaded.</p>
  <div class="runtime-fields">
    <label for="runtime-module">Browser module URL
      <input id="runtime-module" type="text" spellcheck="false" value="{{ '/npm/factoidal/browser.js' | url }}" autocomplete="off">
    </label>
    <label for="runtime-assets">Wasm assets directory <span class="muted">(optional)</span>
      <input id="runtime-assets" type="text" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Default: l4-assets/ beside browser.js" autocomplete="off">
    </label>
    <button id="load-runtime" type="button" class="secondary">Load local runtime</button>
  </div>
  <p id="runtime-status" class="status" role="status">Ready to load. Run a query to load the runtime automatically.</p>
  <details>
    <summary>Use another local build</summary>
    <p>Serve the Hub and the package from the same HTTP origin, normally <code>http://localhost</code>. Point the module field at that package's <code>browser.js</code>. If needed, point the assets field at the directory containing <code>l4factoidal.js</code>, <code>l4factoidal.mjs</code> and <code>l4factoidal.wasm</code>. Reload the page to change an already loaded runtime.</p>
    <p>To build from this repository, run <code>bash formal/lean4/Wasm/build-wasm.sh /tmp/factoidal-gpu-demo-wasm</code> with Lean and Emscripten installed. Serve the site with Eleventy, then set the assets directory to <code>{{ '/web/hub/assets/l4/' | url }}</code>. <a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/docs/web/hub/README.md#mixed-cpu--gpu-sparql-local-runtime-workbench">Full local setup instructions</a>.</p>
    <p>WebGPU needs a supported browser in a secure context. Automatic mode can use the CPU when WebGPU is absent or the adapter is a known software implementation. Required GPU mode reports a refusal when it cannot complete an eligible join on the device.</p>
    <pre id="runtime-info">No runtime loaded.</pre>
  </details>
</section>

<div class="workspace">
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="data-title">
    <div class="panel-title"><h2 id="data-title">2. Dataset</h2><span class="step-note">PARSE ONCE · REUSE</span></div>
    <div class="inline-controls">
      <label for="sample-size">People in the sample
        <select id="sample-size"><option value="64">64 · small</option><option value="2048" selected>2,048 · join-sized</option><option value="8192">8,192 · larger</option></select>
      </label>
      <button id="load-sample" class="secondary" type="button">Use sample</button>
    </div>
    <p>The sample links people to eight projects, with names and optional regions. The larger samples can reach the automatic join threshold; placement still depends on the device.</p>
    <label for="dataset-file">Or open a local RDF file
      <input id="dataset-file" type="file" accept=".ttl,.trig,.nt,.nq,.jsonld,.json,.rdf,.xml,.txt">
    </label>
    <p class="small">The selected file is read in this page. It is not uploaded.</p>
    <label for="dataset-format">Input format
      <select id="dataset-format"><option value="">Detect in the engine</option><option value="turtle" selected>Turtle</option><option value="trig">TriG</option><option value="ntriples">N-Triples</option><option value="nquads">N-Quads</option><option value="jsonld">JSON-LD</option><option value="rdfxml">RDF/XML</option></select>
    </label>
    <label for="dataset-text">Editable RDF source
      <textarea id="dataset-text" rows="12" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off"></textarea>
    </label>
    <button id="load-dataset" class="secondary" type="button">Parse dataset</button>
    <p id="dataset-status" class="status" role="status">The sample is ready to parse.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="query-title">
    <div class="panel-title"><h2 id="query-title">3. Query</h2><span class="step-note">SHIPPING QUERY API</span></div>
    <label for="query-preset">Sample query
      <select id="query-preset"></select>
    </label>
    <label for="query-text">SPARQL <span class="muted">· Ctrl / ⌘ + Enter to run</span>
      <textarea id="query-text" rows="13" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off"></textarea>
    </label>
    <label for="execution-mode">Execution mode
      <select id="execution-mode"><option value="auto">Automatic · choose per join</option><option value="cpu">CPU · existing evaluator</option><option value="gpu">Required GPU · refuse if unavailable</option></select>
    </label>
    <details class="limits">
      <summary>Join limits</summary>
      <div class="inline-controls">
        <label for="gpu-min-rows">Minimum input rows <span class="muted">(optional)</span>
          <input id="gpu-min-rows" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="1" placeholder="Auto: 1024 · GPU: 1">
        </label>
        <label for="gpu-max-pairs">Maximum candidate pairs
          <input id="gpu-max-pairs" type="number" min="0" max="2097120" step="1" value="1000000">
        </label>
      </div>
      <p>The engine checks these limits. In automatic mode, a refused GPU request resumes on the CPU and preserves the full answer.</p>
    </details>
    <div class="actions"><button id="run-query" type="button">Run query</button><button id="compare-cpu" type="button" class="secondary">Run + compare CPU</button></div>
    <p class="small">Automatic placement uses a conservative size estimate. Required GPU mode also allows software adapters for device testing.</p>
  </section>
</div>

