<section class="panel evidence-panel" id="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
  <h2 id="evidence-title">What this run demonstrates</h2>
  <p>This page calls <code>core.query(dataset, query, options)</code>. The engine owns SPARQL parsing, join placement, RDF matching and query modifiers. The host transports the emitted GPU plans and displays the answer. The CPU comparison is a separate run of the same public API.</p>
  <p>The checked numeric readback and pure mixed plan have Lean proofs against the reference answer. The registry retains an explicit IO assumption for the stateful session and ABI, which are covered by integration tests. Browser, driver and hardware speed is measured, not proved.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/docs/designissues/2026-11-22-mixed-gpu-sparql.md">Architecture and proof boundary</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/npm/factoidal/README.md#mixed-cpuwebgpu-sparql">Query API</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/tools/pvgraph-query-device-smoke.mjs">Device integration tests</a></p>
  <details><summary>Live registry entry: <code>gpuSparqlStage</code></summary><pre id="registry-json">Load the runtime to read its shipping registry.</pre></details>
</section>
